    "custom_liquid_kgwc6a": {
      "type": "custom-liquid",
      "name": "t:sections.custom-liquid.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "custom_liquid": "<section id=\"collection-faq-section\" class=\"faq-container\" aria-labelledby=\"collection-faq-title\">\n<h2 id=\"collection-faq-title\" class=\"faq-title\">Nearsighted Snorkel Mask FAQ</h2>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">What is a nearsighted snorkel mask?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>A nearsighted prescription snorkel dive mask is designed for people who need minus-power vision correction underwater. Instead of standard flat glass, these masks use prescription lenses that help distant objects appear clearer while snorkeling or scuba diving. They are a popular choice for divers with myopia who want a more natural underwater viewing experience, especially when searching for a reliable snorkel mask for nearsighted swimmers.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">Can I use a nearsighted swim mask for both snorkeling and scuba diving?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>Yes. Most prescription snorkeling and scuba masks are designed to perform well in both environments. Tempered glass lenses, reliable seals, and durable silicone skirts help maintain clear vision and comfort whether you stay near the surface or go deeper on a dive.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">How do I choose the correct minus lens strength underwater?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>Most divers start with the Sphere value from their latest glasses prescription and select the closest available minus power. Because water naturally magnifies objects slightly, many people choose lenses that are 0.25 to 0.50 weaker than their everyday glasses for a more comfortable underwater experience.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">Can I choose different prescription strengths for each eye in a snorkel mask?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>Yes. All of our nearsighted prescription snorkel masks allow different lens strengths for each eye. This is especially helpful for swimmers with uneven myopia who need more precise underwater vision correction.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">What makes a comfortable Rx nearsighted mask fit?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>A comfortable shortsighted mask depends on your face shape, skirt softness, and overall mask design. Many snorkelers prefer low-volume masks with soft silicone skirts because they create a secure seal and reduce pressure during longer snorkeling or scuba sessions. A good diving mask for nearsighted users should also keep the prescription lenses stable and clear underwater.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">Are nearsighted prescription snorkel masks suitable for long dives?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>Absolutely. A properly fitted nearsighted prescription snorkel mask can stay comfortable during long dives and extended snorkeling sessions. Soft silicone materials, secure lens positioning, and a leak-resistant seal all help improve comfort and visibility underwater. Many divers look for comfort, clarity, and fit when choosing the best snorkel mask for nearsighted vision.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">Are nearsighted swim masks available in unisex styles?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>Yes. Many prescription masks for nearsighted come in unisex styles designed to fit a wide range of face shapes comfortably. Different frame designs, skirt sizes, and adjustable straps make it easier to find the right comfortable fit for both comfort and underwater visibility.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n<details class=\"faq-item\">\n<summary class=\"faq-question\"><h3 style=\"margin: 0;\">What should I do if I order the wrong lenses for my myopia diving mask?</h3></summary>\n<div class=\"faq-answer\">\n<p>If you are unsure about your nearsighted prescription before ordering, it’s best to contact us for guidance first. Our team at Oceans Optics can help verify the correct lens strength for your dive mask and explain our return or exchange policy before you purchase.</p>\n</div>\n</details>\n\n</section>\n\n<script type=\"application/ld+json\">\n{\n\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n\"@type\": \"FAQPage\",\n\"mainEntity\": [\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"What is a nearsighted snorkel mask?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"A nearsighted prescription snorkel dive mask is designed for people who need minus-power vision correction underwater. Instead of standard flat glass, these masks use prescription lenses that help distant objects appear clearer while snorkeling or scuba diving. They are a popular choice for divers with myopia who want a more natural underwater viewing experience, especially when searching for a reliable snorkel mask for nearsighted swimmers.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"Can I use a nearsighted swim mask for both snorkeling and scuba diving?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"Yes. Most prescription snorkeling and scuba masks are designed to perform well in both environments. Tempered glass lenses, reliable seals, and durable silicone skirts help maintain clear vision and comfort whether you stay near the surface or go deeper on a dive.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"How do I choose the right minus lens strength underwater?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"Most divers start with the Sphere value from their latest glasses prescription and select the closest available minus power. Because water naturally magnifies objects slightly, many people choose lenses that are 0.25 to 0.50 weaker than their everyday glasses for a more comfortable underwater experience.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"Can I choose different prescription strengths for each eye in a snorkel mask?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"Yes. All of our nearsighted prescription snorkel masks allow different lens strengths for each eye. This is especially helpful for swimmers with uneven myopia who need more precise underwater vision correction.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"What makes a comfortable Rx nearsighted mask fit?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"A comfortable shortsighted mask depends on your face shape, skirt softness, and overall mask design. Many snorkelers prefer low-volume masks with soft silicone skirts because they create a secure seal and reduce pressure during longer snorkeling or scuba sessions. A good diving mask for nearsighted users should also keep the prescription lenses stable and clear underwater.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"Are nearsighted prescription snorkel masks suitable for long dives?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"Absolutely. A properly fitted nearsighted prescription snorkel mask can stay comfortable during long dives and extended snorkeling sessions. Soft silicone materials, secure lens positioning, and a leak-resistant seal all help improve comfort and visibility underwater. Many divers look for comfort, clarity, and fit when choosing the best snorkel mask for nearsighted vision.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"Are nearsighted swim masks available in unisex styles?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"Yes. Many prescription masks for nearsighted come in unisex styles designed to fit a wide range of face shapes comfortably. Different frame designs, skirt sizes, and adjustable straps make it easier to find the right comfortable fit for both comfort and underwater visibility.\"\n}\n},\n{\n\"@type\": \"Question\",\n\"name\": \"What should I do if I order the wrong lenses for my myopia diving mask?\",\n\"acceptedAnswer\": {\n\"@type\": \"Answer\",\n\"text\": \"If you are unsure about your nearsighted prescription before ordering, it’s best to contact us for guidance first. Our team at Oceans Optics can help verify the correct lens strength for your dive mask and explain our return or exchange policy before you purchase.\"\n}\n}\n]\n}\n</script>\n\n<style>\n.faq-container {\nmax-width: 700px;\nmargin: 20px auto;\npadding: 20px;\nborder-top: 1px solid #023059;\nfont-family: 'Lato', sans-serif;\n}\n.faq-title {\nfont-size: 24px;\nfont-weight: bold;\ncolor: #023059;\ntext-align: center;\nmargin-bottom: 15px;\n}\n.faq-item {\nborder-bottom: 1px solid #ddd;\nmargin-bottom: 10px;\n}\n.faq-question {\nfont-size: 16px;\nbackground-color: #ffffff;\ncolor: #023059;\npadding: 10px;\ncursor: pointer;\nborder: 1px solid #023059;\nborder-radius: 5px;\nmargin: 0;\nfont-weight: 700;\ndisplay: flex;\nalign-items: baseline;\n}\n.faq-question h3 {\nfont-size: 16px;\ncolor: #023059;\nfont-weight: 700;\nmargin: 0;\n}\n.faq-answer {\npadding: 10px;\nfont-size: 14px;\nbackground-color: #f9f9f9;\ncolor: #333;\nfont-weight: 400;\n}\n.faq-answer p { margin: 0 0 8px 0; }\n.faq-answer p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }\n.faq-answer a { color: #B95e05; text-decoration: none; }\n.faq-answer a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }\ndetails summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }\ndetails[open] .faq-question::before { content: \"▾ \"; }\ndetails:not([open]) .faq-question::before { content: \"▸ \"; }\n</style>",
